\ A word returns a quotation whose own body cannot be compiled to native code: it
\ defines a helper word inside the body, which AOT compilation cannot discover.
\ Under strict interpreter-free AOT there is no interpreter to run the escaping
\ body and no runtime image to carry it, so the build fails with a quotation-body
\ diagnostic that points at --emit-runtime-image.
make-q: ( -- q ) [ [ drop helper: [ 7 ] ; helper ] ] ;

0 make-q call drop
